From: Birk Skyum
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: don't count a vdev restart as a started vdev

Upstream proposed patch: https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2610.2/11945.html
This addresses one possible source of an inflated vdev count. It does not
establish that the user's actual timeout has that cause.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -11953,7 +11953,8 @@ ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart(struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif,
 						   &arvif->reg_tpc_info);
 	}
 
-	ar->num_started_vdevs++;
+	if (!restart)
+		ar->num_started_vdevs++;
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_MAC,  "vdev %pM started, vdev_id %d\n",
 		   ahvif->vif->addr, arvif->vdev_id);
 
